{
	"nodes":[
		{"id":"hub","type":"text","text":"CAT7 — Semantic checking is valued\nRQ3 · finding","x":140,"y":-80,"width":400,"height":100,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"cases","type":"text","text":"Cases\nL1 L2 L3 L4 S2 S3 S4 S5 S6","x":-220,"y":-80,"width":300,"height":70,"color":"3"},
		{"id":"memo_group","type":"text","text":"**Memos** (7) — Ctrl+hover a link to preview\n\n- [[S3M4]] — Bizagi scaffolds vocabulary and syntax\n- [[S4M5]] — tool semantics and workplace informality diverge from class\n- [[S5M4]] — AI and live tools in the group modelling loop\n- [[S6M3]] — examples and attendance carry abstraction norms\n- [[L1M5]] — proper tools versus draw.io in teaching stance\n- [[L3M1]] — executable models as learning and grading infrastructure\n- [[L4M5]] — whiteboard compensates for missing integrated tools","x":-380,"y":200,"width":520,"height":276,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"code_group","type":"text","text":"**Codes** (23) — Ctrl+hover a link to preview\n\n- [[L1-C17]] — prefers modelling tools over generic drawing tools\n- [[L1-C18]] — tool licensing pushes lecturer to switch tools\n- [[L1-C20]] — wants more tool time and examples in class\n- [[L1-C21]] — ideal tool would give feedback and next steps\n- [[L3-C03]] — executable UML validates student models for grading\n- [[L3-C04]] — executable models make modeling feel dynamic for learning\n- [[L3-C06]] — tool chosen for semantic checking and grading support\n- [[L4-C16]] — expensive tools limit access and integration\n- [[L4-C26]] — missing integrated tools drives whiteboard use\n- [[L4-C27]] — piStar semantic checking is valued for iStar\n- [[L4-C28]] — switching tools across families creates friction\n- [[L4-C29]] — wants lightweight integrated cross-paradigm tool\n- [[S3-C14]] — Bizagi vocabulary in UI helped learning\n- [[S3-C15]] — tool hover hints helped beginners start\n- [[S3-C16]] — large diagrams slow and can corrupt on save\n- [[S4-C01]] — informal sketches outside formal UML coursework\n- [[S4-C12]] — ChatGPT useful as explainer not model generator\n- [[S4-C13]] — semantic tools help learning invalid sketch tools\n- [[S5-C10]] — AI suggests options then team rewrites manually\n- [[S5-C11]] — live Miro editing lowered group modelling barrier\n- [[S5-C12]] — passive teammates block motivation regardless of domain\n- [[S6-C04]] — worked examples set acceptable abstraction levels\n- [[S6-C12]] — separate tools and missed tutorial blocked NFR progress","x":560,"y":200,"width":520,"height":724,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"explainer","type":"text","text":"What this means\n\nPeople value tools that check whether a model is valid — not just blank drawing boards that accept anything.","x":80,"y":-340,"width":520,"height":150,"color":"1"}
